      "definicion_pragmatica": "In negatives and questions, 'do/does' carries the grammar, so the main verb goes back to its base form: 'She doesn't drive', 'Does she drive?' — never 'doesn't drives'.",
      "tabla": {
        "titulo": "Do / Does — the auxiliary does the work",
        "encabezados": ["Form", "Structure", "Example"],
